{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S4: Config-driven link-relation mapping, skip-not-approximate preserved\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nEpic 3d7a adds a config-driven mapping seam. S1 landed core `mapping_config.py`\n(`MappingLayer` with `link_map: Mapping[str,str]`, `SKIP=\"skip\"`,\n`resolve_for_project`, `validate`, `Capability`). S2 made STATUS config-driven\n(`config.py:77`). S4 does the same for rebar-relation → Jira-link mapping,\npreserving \"skip, don't approximate\": map to a real declared project link type, or\nskip — never invent an approximate link. S4 is link-relation ONLY (priority is S5;\ntype/parents out of scope).\n\nLink emission has TWO halves in `outbound_links.py`, only on the UPDATE path\n(`outbound_mutation_builders.py:285`; creates emit no links):\n\n- ADD — `_diff_links` (`outbound_links.py:34`): per local dep, calls\n  `links.link_payload_for_relation(relation)` (`:83`) and skips on `None` (`:84`).\n- REMOVE — `_diff_link_removals` (`outbound_links.py:120`): walks the REMOTE\n  canonical set `links.map_remote_links(jira_fields)` — `(relation, other_key,\n  opaque_vendor_type)` — emitting `{\"action\":\"remove\",\"type\":opaque_vendor_type,...}`\n  (`:150`) for a managed, locally-absent link, stopping the inbound differ re-adding a\n  deliberate local unlink each pass (the churn).\n\nCRITICAL for REMOVE: each remote link's `relation` is recovered from its ACTUAL\nremote vendor type by the BUILT-IN, config-unaware reverse map\n`link_direction.JIRA_LINK_TO_RELATION` via `resolve_inbound_link`\n(`link_direction.py:19,27`) — `{\"Blocks\":\"blocks\",\"Relates\":\"relates_to\"}`. A type\nNOT in that map reverses to `relation=None`, so a REMAPPED (overridden) remote type is\nsilently dropped unless attribution is config-aware — this story's core REMOVE fix.\n\nBoth `link_payload_for_relation` impls read built-in `RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK`\ndirectly in TWO backends: `adapters/jira/backend.py:323`,\n`adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:527`. `RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK: dict[str,\ntuple[str, bool]]` (`value_maps.py:104`): `blocks→(Blocks,False)`,\n`depends_on→(Blocks,True)`, `relates_to→(Relates,False)`; unsynced in\n`UNSYNCED_RELATIONS` (`value_maps.py:128`). TYPE MISMATCH: built-in payload is a\n`(link_type, swap)` TUPLE; the S1 `link_map` axis is flat `str→str`.\n\n## Approach\n\nMirror S2's forward seam; apply ONE effective link map to ADD and REMOVE, with\nconfig-aware REMOVE attribution.\n\n1. **`config.effective_link_map(project_key, root)`** (`config.py`, NEW), like\n   `effective_status_map` (`config.py:77`). Add an adapter-free literal\n   `local_to_jira_link` = `{\"blocks\":\"Blocks\",\"depends_on\":\"Blocks\",\n   \"relates_to\":\"Relates\"}` (link-TYPE only; parity-tested like `local_to_jira_status`).\n   Build `builtin = mc.MappingLayer(link_map=local_to_jira_link)`,\n   `mc.resolve_for_project`, `mc.validate(resolved, mc.Capability(has_link_types=True))`\n   (fail-closed), return `resolved.link_map` **retaining `SKIP`** so a\n   forced skip ≠ an absent key.\n\n2. **One resolver, both directions.** Add `_effective_link_map_for(ticket, mapping,\n   repo_root)` in `outbound_differ.py` (NEW, sibling of `_effective_status_map_for`,\n   `:272`). Compute once at `outbound_mutation_builders.py:285`; pass the SAME\n   `link_map: Mapping[str,str] | None = None` to BOTH diff funcs. Shared helper\n   `_resolve_link(relation, links, link_map) -> tuple[str,bool] | None` unifies both.\n\n3. **`_resolve_link`:** `override = link_map.get(relation)`; `override == SKIP` →\n   `None`; `payload = links.link_payload_for_relation(relation)`; `override` a `str` →\n   `(override, payload[1] if payload else False)` (overrides only link_type; built-in\n   swap preserved, `False` default); else → `payload` (maybe `None` → skip).\n\n   **ADD** (`_diff_links`): `_resolve_link`; `None` ⇒ `continue`; else emit\n   `type=vendor_type, swap=swap`. No `[mapping]` ⇒ both paths byte-for-byte today.\n\n   **REMOVE** (`_diff_link_removals`): config-aware attribution FIRST. Build\n   `reverse = {v: k for k, v in link_map.items() if v != SKIP}`. For each canonical\n   `(relation, other_key, opaque_vendor_type)`:\n   - `relation is None` (built-in `JIRA_LINK_TO_RELATION` didn't know this remote\n     type) ⇒ recover `relation = reverse.get(opaque_vendor_type)`; still `None` ⇒\n     genuinely unmapped ⇒ `continue` (adopt). This stops a remapped link being dropped.\n   - `_resolve_link(relation, ...)` is `None` (SKIP) ⇒ `continue` — suppress REMOVE (a\n     skipped relation is neither added nor removed; no inbound re-add).\n   - else keep/remove as today against `(relation, local_target)` in `local_deps` /\n     `managed_refs`, emitting `type=opaque_vendor_type` — the ACTUAL remote type,\n     which IS the overridden type when remapped (no re-substitution), so add\n     and remove reference ONE type.\n\n4. **Fail-closed on undeclared link type.** The S1 mechanism exists\n   (`MappingLayer.link_types` `mapping_config.py:102`, `Capability.has_link_types`\n   `:80`, `validate()`'s `_check_vocab(link_map, link_types)` `:359`) but `validate()`\n   is not yet invoked. A project declares `[mapping.default] link_types = [...]`;\n   `effective_link_map` calling `validate()` (NEW) raises `MappingConfigError` on a\n   `link_map` value outside it. `SKIP` always allowed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `config.py`: `local_to_jira_link` literal + `effective_link_map` (~130 LOC).\n- `outbound_differ.py`: `_effective_link_map_for`.\n- `outbound_links.py`: `link_map` arg + shared `_resolve_link` + config-aware\n  `reverse` attribution on both diff funcs (~220 LOC).\n- `outbound_mutation_builders.py`: compute + pass `link_map` at `:285`.\n- Backends + `link_direction.py` UNCHANGED (config-awareness layers in the removal\n  path; the built-in reverse map stays the direction-aware first attempt).\n- NEW `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_link_mapping.py`.\n- OUT of scope: parents (S7), priority (S5), type axis, inbound remap-awareness.\n- All modules stay well under the 800-LOC hard cap.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_link_mapping.py` (`pytestmark =\npytest.mark.unit`), driving REAL entry points (`config.effective_link_map`,\n`_diff_links`, `_diff_link_removals`) via a tmp `rebar.toml` `[mapping]` block:\n\n- `test_link_config_effect` — a `link_map` override (`relates_to = \"Relationship\"`)\n  changes the ADD mutation's `type` while preserving built-in `swap`; AND on REMOVE, a\n  managed, locally-absent remote link carrying \"Relationship\" is config-awarely\n  attributed to `relates_to` (not dropped) and emits a remove with `type=\n  \"Relationship\"`. No `[mapping]` ⇒ both paths unchanged.\n- `test_link_skip_preserved` — a `\"skip\"` override (and an unsynced relation) emits NO\n  ADD; the same skip suppresses the REMOVE — never added nor removed; no approximate\n  link substituted.\n- `test_link_undeclared_fails_closed` — a `link_map` value outside a declared\n  `link_types` vocabulary makes `effective_link_map` raise `MappingConfigError`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The SAME effective `link_map` governs ADD and REMOVE via one `_resolve_link`;\n      ADD composes override link_type + built-in swap; verified by\n      `test_link_config_effect`.\n- [ ] Skip is symmetric: a `\"skip\"` override (and unsynced relations) suppress BOTH\n      ADD and REMOVE — never added nor removed; verified by `test_link_skip_preserved`.\n- [ ] REMOVE attribution is config-aware: a remote link carrying an OVERRIDDEN vendor\n      type is attributed via the inverted map, NOT spuriously dropped/adopted, and its\n      remove targets that same overridden type; verified by `test_link_config_effect`.\n- [ ] Undeclared link type fails closed via `validate()`; verified by\n      `test_link_undeclared_fails_closed`.\n- [ ] Both consumers (`jira/backend.py:323`, `jira_datacenter/backend.py:527`) route\n      through the single `effective_link_map` seam; no `[mapping]` block leaves\n      emission unchanged; a parity test keeps `config.local_to_jira_link` in lock-step\n      with `RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK`'s link-type components.\n\nTest tier: unit"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787356373372219001,"uuid":"b78f0a28-493c-4a30-b974-21b022b6e806"}